# TARS — Cursor AI rules

This file is the legacy-format snapshot of `CLAUDE.md` and
`.cursor/rules/tars-architecture.mdc`. Keep all three in sync.

> Naming: product = **TARS**. Older copies may say "Jarvis"; rename to TARS
> when editing. Folder name `Jarvis/jarvis` stays so existing paths keep
> working.

## What this project is

- TARS is the local-first "Neural Cockpit" agent. Released under the
  `meeet.world` brand with cross-cutting trace logging via the meeet bridge.
- Backend: Python, FastAPI-style routers under `web_extras/routers/`. Domain
  subsystems in `backend/core/*`. Agent and MCP entry points in
  `backend/agents/` and `backend/mcp/`.
- Frontend canon: vanilla HTML/CSS/JS in `frontend/` — no React, no Tailwind,
  no bundler.
- Premium marketing surfaces:
  - `experiments/neural-showcase-v2/` — Vite + Three.js + GSAP + Lenis +
    postprocessing. WebGL + custom GLSL. Port 5173.
  - `experiments/neural-showcase-v3/` — React + Vite + Tailwind v4 +
    framer-motion + shadcn-style `components.json` ready for 21st.dev
    drops. Port 5174.
  These are the only places where heavier frontend deps live; do not
  bleed them into `frontend/`.

## Awareness layer

`backend/core/awareness/` is load-bearing (calendar / memory / code_index /
mac_actions). Do not refactor without explicit scope.

## Domain packs (Phase 9)

`backend/core/domains/` is a plugin system with built-in packs:
`traders`, `business`, `mlm`, `science`.

- Base: `backend/core/domains/base.py` (`DomainPack`, `DomainManifest`,
  `ActionSpec`, `AwarenessSource`).
- Registry: `backend/core/domains/registry.py`.
- Packs: `backend/core/domains/packs/{slug}/{pack,actions,awareness,prompts}.py`.
- HTTP: `web_extras/routers/domains.py` mounts at `/api/domains`.
- Tests: `tests/test_domains.py`, `tests/test_meeet.py`.
- Spec: `docs/DOMAIN_PACKS.md`.

Action handlers must be `async`, return a dict with `ok`, never raise on bad
user input, never auto-execute destructive ops.

## meeet.world bridge (Phase 9.1)

`backend/core/meeet/` — stdlib-only end-to-end logging.

- `start_trace` / `current_trace` / `trace_scope` for context.
- `MeeetClient.emit(kind, payload)` for events.
- Env: `MEEET_INGEST_URL`, `MEEET_CONTRACT_VERSION` (default `1.0.0`),
  `MEEET_API_KEY`, `MEEET_SOURCE`, `MEEET_LOCAL_LOG`.
- The domain router runs every action invocation in a `trace_scope` and emits
  `domain.action.invoked|completed|failed`. It accepts an upstream
  `x-meeet-trace-id` header for cross-service propagation.

## Frontend conventions

- Vanilla in `frontend/`. Use existing CSS tokens (`--indigo`, `--violet`,
  `--cyan`, `--white`, `--dim`, `--faint`, `--border`, `--shadow`, `--rad-md`,
  `--rad-lg`, `--font-body`, `--font-mono`).
- Aesthetic: minimalism + futurism. No rainbow gradients, no neon flooding.
- Cockpit/operator pages keep the dark HUD aesthetic.
- Marketing/landing pages evolve toward premium AI-product feel.
- Always implement empty / loading / error / success states for async surfaces.
- Animations via CSS transitions/keyframes; avoid heavy JS animation libs.
- Accessibility: semantic structure, focus rings, `aria-live` for async.

## Showcase v2 conventions

- WebGL scene under `src/scene/`. Custom GLSL in `src/scene/shaders/`.
- Postprocessing: tame bloom + faint CA + vignette + noise + SMAA.
- Palette: deep ink + soft pastel cyan + warm amber (no neon rainbow).
- A single subtle telemetry panel (`aside.hud`) top-left only.
- Drop a GLB at `public/models/brain.glb` to override the procedural reactor.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` everywhere.

## Backend conventions

- New endpoints in `web_extras/routers/`, follow existing patterns.
- Don't change response shapes silently; additive keys are fine.
- Background / long-running tasks: `backend/core/background` + observability.

## Engineering guardrails

- Scoped changes only.
- No npm tooling outside `experiments/`.
- Never commit `.env`.
- Flag any cross-stack change.
- For "innovative design" requests: produce a plan before big refactors.

## Design system & skill

- Source of truth: `design-system/tars/MASTER.md`. Pages: `design-system/tars/pages/<slug>.md`.
- Skill `nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill` installed in three places:
  `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` (Cursor),
  `.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` (Claude Code project),
  `~/.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` (Claude Code global). Auto-activates
  on UI/UX work.
- Targeted lookup:
  `python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py "<query>"
  --domain style|landing|typography|ux|color`.
- One cyan accent only (`#67E8F9`); amber (`#FBBF24`) reserved for live
  telemetry. No AI-purple/pink rainbow gradients.

## 21st.dev workflow

`experiments/neural-showcase-v3/` is the React drop-zone. Add any 21st.dev
block from inside that folder:
`npx shadcn@latest add "https://21st.dev/r/<author>/<id>"`.
Components land in `src/components/ui/` and inherit our tokens via
shadcn CSS variables in `src/index.css`.

## Sync with the agent

`docs/AGENT_HANDOFF.md` lists current state and pending work.
`docs/CHANGELOG_AGENTS.md` is the per-edit log.
`docs/IDEAS.md` is the proposals queue.
`design-system/tars/MASTER.md` is the visual source of truth.
Read all four when starting fresh.
